Haakon Studebaker <heptapod@gmail.com> writes:

> ../util/panic.c:55: warning: conflicting types for built-in function 
> 'alloca'
> Linking ../util/lev_comp.exe...
> ../util/dgn_comp.y has changed. To update dgn_yacc.c and
> ../include/dgn_comp.h run byacc.

The alloca function in panic.c is within an #ifdef ALLOCA_HACK block.
And in front of it there is a comment like this:

/*
 * In case bison-generated foo_yacc.c tries to use alloca(); if we don't
 * have it then just use malloc() instead.  This may not work on some
 * systems, but they should either use yacc or get a real alloca routine.
 */

This seems to indicate that you have ALLOCA_HACK defined but shouldn't.
And in your case, ALLOCA_HACK is most likely defined in include/ntconf.h
which defines it if "alloca" is not defined:

#ifndef alloca
#define ALLOCA_HACK     /* used in util/panic.c */
#endif

Hmm.. you could TRY commenting out the middle line above from
include/ntconf.h and see if that helps.
But I suspect that there's actually something else wrong in your setup and
this may bring you some other error.

